<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 19.17 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 19.17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 52 basis points to 19.17 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     19.69	    19.17		   - 52 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     22.14	    21.61		   - 53 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    22.75	    22.46		   - 29 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.99	    23.50		   - 49 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST/2330 GMT.</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
